WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:02.775
Hello and welcome back to J D Science.

2
00:00:02.949 --> 00:00:06.803
In today's T-Level Chemistry lesson, we are going to study

3
00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:10.252
A twelve point two, Calculating Rate of Reaction.

4
00:00:10.588 --> 00:00:14.013
By the end of this lesson, you should be able to calculate

5
00:00:14.071 --> 00:00:17.775
average rate from tables and graphs, using amount of

6
00:00:17.845 --> 00:00:21.479
reactant used or product formed divided by time,

7
00:00:21.815 --> 00:00:23.812
and give the correct compound unit.

8
00:00:24.021 --> 00:00:27.702
Reaction rate is how quickly reactants are used or products

9
00:00:27.748 --> 00:00:28.433
are formed.

10
00:00:28.677 --> 00:00:32.415
Average rate over a chosen interval is the change in

11
00:00:32.473 --> 00:00:34.668
amount divided by the time taken.

12
00:00:35.004 --> 00:00:38.696
Amount may be mass in grams, gas volume in cubic

13
00:00:38.754 --> 00:00:42.934
centimetres or cubic decimetres, or amount in moles.

14
00:00:43.178 --> 00:00:44.606
Use the units given.

15
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.576
Do not convert unless the question requires it or the

16
00:00:48.692 --> 00:00:50.468
units are inconsistent.

17
00:00:50.712 --> 00:00:54.834
If a reactant amount decreases, the amount used is initial

18
00:00:54.915 --> 00:00:55.983
minus final.

19
00:00:56.192 --> 00:00:57.992
That change must be positive.

20
00:00:58.235 --> 00:01:00.232
Rate units are compound units.

21
00:01:00.383 --> 00:01:01.568
Grams per second.

22
00:01:01.742 --> 00:01:03.727
Cubic centimetres per second.

23
00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:05.143
Moles per second.

24
00:01:05.352 --> 00:01:08.952
If time is in minutes, the rate is per minute unless you

25
00:01:09.022 --> 00:01:09.707
convert.

26
00:01:10.101 --> 00:01:12.365
One minute equals sixty seconds.

27
00:01:12.609 --> 00:01:13.654
Worked example.

28
00:01:14.049 --> 00:01:17.659
Seventy two cubic centimetres of gas form in twenty four

29
00:01:17.718 --> 00:01:18.379
seconds.

30
00:01:18.716 --> 00:01:22.478
Seventy two divided by twenty four is three point zero

31
00:01:22.571 --> 00:01:24.603
cubic centimetres per second.

32
00:01:24.846 --> 00:01:28.596
The same method gives three point zero cubic centimetres per

33
00:01:28.643 --> 00:01:32.451
second for forty five cubic centimetres in fifteen seconds,

34
00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:36.352
and for eighty four cubic centimetres in twenty eight seconds.

35
00:01:36.526 --> 00:01:38.511
Now a reactant example.

36
00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:42.563
A solid falls from eight point four zero grams to six

37
00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:45.454
point nine zero grams in fifty seconds.

38
00:01:45.791 --> 00:01:48.449
The change is one point five zero grams.

39
00:01:48.693 --> 00:01:52.652
One point five zero divided by fifty is zero point zero

40
00:01:52.722 --> 00:01:54.567
three zero grams per second.

41
00:01:54.846 --> 00:01:55.810
Check another.

42
00:01:56.053 --> 00:02:00.129
Twelve point five grams to ten point one grams in eighty seconds.

43
00:02:00.372 --> 00:02:02.555
The change is two point four grams.

44
00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:06.491
Two point four divided by eighty is also zero point

45
00:02:06.549 --> 00:02:08.929
zero three zero grams per second.

46
00:02:09.324 --> 00:02:10.485
Time conversion.

47
00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:14.258
Two point five minutes is one hundred and fifty seconds.

48
00:02:14.409 --> 00:02:18.252
One hundred and twenty cubic centimetres in two point zero minutes

49
00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:20.736
is sixty cubic centimetres per minute.

50
00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:24.799
Two point zero minutes is one hundred and twenty seconds, so

51
00:02:24.869 --> 00:02:28.909
the rate is also one point zero cubic centimetre per second.

52
00:02:29.304 --> 00:02:30.326
Now a table.

53
00:02:30.604 --> 00:02:34.807
Gas volume is zero at zero seconds, eighteen at twenty seconds,

54
00:02:35.051 --> 00:02:39.184
forty two at fifty seconds, and fifty eight at eighty seconds.

55
00:02:39.579 --> 00:02:43.434
From twenty to fifty seconds the change is twenty four cubic

56
00:02:43.492 --> 00:02:45.593
centimetres in thirty seconds.

57
00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:50.109
Twenty four divided by thirty is zero point eight zero

58
00:02:50.191 --> 00:02:52.071
cubic centimetres per second.

59
00:02:52.524 --> 00:02:56.541
From fifty to eighty seconds the change is sixteen cubic

60
00:02:56.588 --> 00:03:00.454
centimetres in thirty seconds, which is zero point five

61
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.297
three cubic centimetres per second to two significant

62
00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:05.005
figures.

63
00:03:05.342 --> 00:03:07.327
The first interval is faster.

64
00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:11.309
On a product-time graph, average rate is the gradient

65
00:03:11.379 --> 00:03:15.082
of the chord between two points: vertical change

66
00:03:15.152 --> 00:03:17.102
divided by horizontal change.

67
00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:21.526
From eighteen cubic centimetres at twenty seconds to forty

68
00:03:21.595 --> 00:03:25.485
two cubic centimetres at fifty seconds, the chord is again

69
00:03:25.566 --> 00:03:29.223
twenty-four over thirty, zero point eight zero

70
00:03:29.293 --> 00:03:31.429
cubic centimetres per second.

71
00:03:31.882 --> 00:03:35.748
An examination graph uses fifteen cubic centimetres at

72
00:03:35.794 --> 00:03:39.474
twenty seconds and thirty nine cubic centimetres at

73
00:03:39.533 --> 00:03:40.531
sixty seconds.

74
00:03:41.146 --> 00:03:45.117
The change is twenty four cubic centimetres in forty seconds,

75
00:03:45.512 --> 00:03:49.506
so the rate is zero point six zero cubic centimetres

76
00:03:49.575 --> 00:03:50.284
per second.

77
00:03:50.678 --> 00:03:52.513
Correct three common errors.

78
00:03:52.907 --> 00:03:56.704
Eighty cubic centimetres in twenty seconds is four cubic

79
00:03:56.762 --> 00:04:00.280
centimetres per second, not four cubic centimetres.

80
00:04:00.732 --> 00:04:02.637
The unit must include time.

81
00:04:02.973 --> 00:04:06.839
If mass falls from nine point zero grams to seven point

82
00:04:06.897 --> 00:04:10.717
five grams in thirty seconds, do not divide seven point

83
00:04:10.763 --> 00:04:11.878
five by thirty.

84
00:04:12.214 --> 00:04:16.104
The change is one point five grams, so the rate is zero

85
00:04:16.185 --> 00:04:18.727
point zero five zero grams per second.

86
00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:22.907
Ninety cubic centimetres in one point five minutes

87
00:04:22.977 --> 00:04:26.820
is sixty cubic centimetres per minute, or one point

88
00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:31.150
zero cubic centimetre per second, not sixty cubic centimetres

89
00:04:31.243 --> 00:04:31.928
per second.

90
00:04:32.457 --> 00:04:35.592
Compare rates only when the units are compatible.

91
00:04:35.986 --> 00:04:37.786
Convert first if needed.

92
00:04:38.065 --> 00:04:39.992
Examination-style question.

93
00:04:40.143 --> 00:04:40.828
Part a.

94
00:04:41.106 --> 00:04:45.123
Ninety six cubic centimetres form in thirty two seconds.

95
00:04:45.332 --> 00:04:46.493
Calculate the rate.

96
00:04:46.702 --> 00:04:47.538
Two marks.

97
00:04:47.817 --> 00:04:51.462
Ninety-six divided by thirty-two is three point

98
00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.970
zero cubic centimetres per second.

99
00:04:54.353 --> 00:04:55.084
Part b.

100
00:04:55.421 --> 00:04:59.078
Mass falls from six point eight zero grams to

101
00:04:59.194 --> 00:05:02.724
five point three zero grams in seventy five seconds.

102
00:05:03.177 --> 00:05:04.047
Three marks.

103
00:05:04.384 --> 00:05:06.996
The change is one point five zero grams.

104
00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:10.885
One point five zero divided by seventy five is zero

105
00:05:10.955 --> 00:05:13.602
point zero two zero grams per second.

106
00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:15.193
Part c.

107
00:05:15.529 --> 00:05:19.233
A graph is read as fifteen cubic centimetres at twenty

108
00:05:19.303 --> 00:05:23.389
seconds and thirty nine cubic centimetres at sixty seconds.

109
00:05:23.668 --> 00:05:24.504
Three marks.

110
00:05:24.585 --> 00:05:28.323
Twenty four cubic centimetres in forty seconds is zero

111
00:05:28.405 --> 00:05:31.760
point six zero cubic centimetres per second.

112
00:05:32.213 --> 00:05:32.851
Part d.

113
00:05:33.188 --> 00:05:34.929
Why is the unit essential?

114
00:05:35.208 --> 00:05:35.963
One mark.

115
00:05:36.172 --> 00:05:40.282
The unit identifies the amount measured and the time basis.

116
00:05:40.619 --> 00:05:42.813
Before we finish, complete the method.

117
00:05:42.987 --> 00:05:44.914
Find the start and end values.

118
00:05:45.042 --> 00:05:46.424
Calculate the change.

119
00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:48.095
Find the time interval.

120
00:05:48.304 --> 00:05:49.860
Divide change by time.

121
00:05:50.034 --> 00:05:52.786
Write the compound unit and round sensibly.

